## Publish lifecycle gates (frozen — P5-B-N-004)

On tour PATCH, after merge + validation, `CanonicalTourService.updateTour` calls `assertTourPublishLifecycleOnUpdate` before persist:

```text
existing.canonical + merged patch
  → runPreTransactionValidation
  → assertTourPublishLifecycleOnUpdate (LC-04)
  → persistTourUpdateAtomically
```

| Assert | Behavior |
|--------|----------|
| LC-04 | Publish/unpublish PATCH invokes lifecycle transition assert |
| LC-05 | Rejected transition → `TourLifecycleTransitionError` → HTTP 400 |
| LC-06 | Golden Denali draft→active publish passes on package path |

Implementation: `assert-tour-publish-lifecycle-gate.ts` maps canonical `publishStatus` (`draft`/`active`) to plugin lifecycle states (`DRAFT`/`OPEN`) via `readTourPublishStatusLabel` → codegen bindings (WAC-001). No direct Denali imports or `workspaceType === "denali"` branches.

Spec: `apps/api/test/tour-publish-transition.spec.ts`.

---

## Draft vs publish validation (frozen — P5-B-N-005)

`ValidateBeforePersistInput.validationMode` (`draft` | `publish`) controls publish-readiness strictness after platform-core `validateCanonical`:

| Mode | Behavior | Assert |
|------|----------|--------|
| `draft` | Skips publish-readiness matrix | VAL-01 |
| `publish` | Runs `wizardHost.validatePublishReadiness` with `publishTransition: true` | VAL-02 |

When omitted, mode is inferred from canonical `publishStatus` via `readTourPublishStatusLabel` (`active`/`published` → `publish`, else `draft`) — WAC-001 binding dispatch, not identity branches.

Implementation: `resolve-validation-mode.ts` · `denali-wizard-rules-module-sync.ts` · wired in `canonical-validation-sync.ts`.

Spec: `apps/api/test/canonical-validation-draft-vs-publish.spec.ts` (VAL-01..03).

