## Form profile strip (frozen — P5-B-N-007)

Server-side strip removes **top-level** Denali tour-kind alias ghosts (`duration`, `eventVariant`, `summitPoint`, `campPoint`, `endPoint`) before `createCanonicalDocument` in pre-TX validation — parity with client `shouldPersistCanonicalPathFromForm` / sanitize ghost purge. Nested composite dependents (`program.shortDescription`, `pricing.basePricePerPerson`, …) remain in canonical ingress from `prepareDenaliSubmitArtifact`.

| Assert | Behavior |
|--------|----------|
| VAL-02b-01 | `duration` / `eventVariant` / dependent nested paths stripped |
| VAL-02b-02 | Non-denali workspace no-op |
| VAL-02b-03 | `stripFormProfileForSubmit` rebuilds canonical document |
| VAL-02b-04 | Plugin ingress roots filtered after strip (duration/eventVariant removed) |

Implementation: `strip-form-profile-for-submit.ts` · wired in `canonical-validation-sync.ts`.

Spec: `apps/api/test/form-profile-strip.spec.ts` (VAL-02b-01..05).

Note: N-005 publish-strict asserts remain **VAL-02** in `canonical-validation-draft-vs-publish.spec.ts`; profile strip band is **VAL-02b** to avoid ID collision.

